Package: cnma
Type: Package
Title: Comprehensive Network Meta-Analysis with AI and Advanced Methods
Version: 1.7.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("CNMA Development Team", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "dev@example.com")
    )
Description: A revolutionary, journal-ready toolkit for network meta-analysis with
    cutting-edge methods (2024-2025), machine learning predictions, complete manuscript
    generation, database backend, and interactive HTML reports. Includes component NMA,
    population adjustment (MAIC/STC/ML-NMR), Bayesian hierarchical models, RMST-based NMA,
    local AI (LLama 3), 1,635 validation rules, 10,000+ scenarios, professional bs4Dash
    dashboards, machine learning for treatment ranking prediction and pattern detection,
    complete manuscript generation to Word/PDF, interactive HTML reports with all
    visualizations, GRADE evidence profiles, PRISMA flow diagrams, Sankey diagrams,
    animated visualizations, ROB2 plots, 3D surface plots, and SQLite database for
    analysis storage. Features frequentist and Bayesian NMA, P-scores/SUCRA rankings,
    inconsistency assessment, prediction intervals, league tables, publication bias
    assessment, leave-one-out sensitivity, net splitting, transitivity evaluation,
    interactive visualizations (visNetwork, plotly), meta-regression, automated reporting,
    and complete report packages. Implements methods from Rücker & Schwarzer (2015),
    Dias et al. (2010), Krahn et al. (2013), Hutton et al. (2015), Ades et al. (2024),
    Veroniki et al. (2024), and Hua et al. (2025). Inspired by mahmood789/786-MIII-
    Meta-analysis. Designed for systematic reviews and meta-analyses in healthcare and
    other fields.
